<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Cleartext is permitted in general, because the watch talks to a gateway whose
  address the user types on the watch.

  An earlier version of this file claimed to permit "private ranges only" and
  listed localhost, 127.0.0.1 and the emulator alias 10.0.2.2. A network
  security config cannot express a CIDR range, so in practice *every* real LAN
  address was refused:

      CLEARTEXT communication to 192.168.1.96 not permitted by network security policy

  which meant the app could not connect to a gateway on a network at all.
  Pinning addresses individually is not possible either: the host is whatever
  the user entered.

  The app's only network traffic is that one socket, so this exception is narrow
  in practice rather than a general hole. It is also deliberate rather than
  temporary: the client builds ``ws://`` unconditionally, so serving the gateway
  over TLS would need a client change first. Until then, run the gateway on a
  network you trust.
-->
<network-security-config>
    <base-config cleartextTrafficPermitted="true" />
</network-security-config>
